WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.299
Everyone's favorite frightening doll is back,
and we're not talking about Chucky.

00:00:05.299 --> 00:00:08.790
We're talking about Annabelle, the messed-up
face of the Conjuring universe.

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:13.260
According to critics, this creepy toy's third
spinoff movie, Annabelle Comes Home, looks

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:15.680
like another big winner for the horror franchise.

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.080
Congratulations, Annabelle!

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:23.440
While there was a moratorium on full reviews
being published in the lead-up to the movie's

00:00:23.449 --> 00:00:27.529
release, Annabelle Comes Home was screened
in advance for a few select critics, and their

00:00:27.529 --> 00:00:30.170
early reactions on Twitter were pretty positive.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:31.529
The general consensus?

00:00:31.529 --> 00:00:35.980
Series writer Gary Dauberman, making his directorial
debut with this threequel, has delivered an

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:40.080
atmospheric, creepy thrill ride that easily
bests the previous Annabelle flicks in terms

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:41.570
of flat-out fun.

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:46.260
Rather than focusing on the doll's origins
in decades past like the previous two films,

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:50.780
Annabelle Comes Home brings things, well,
home, tying itself in with the original Conjuring

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:54.020
series much more closely than the spinoff
series has before.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:58.370
The movie prominently features the demonologists
Lorraine and Ed Warren, the main characters

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:00.370
in The Conjuring and its sequel.

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:04.140
Annabelle Comes Home chronicles the terrifying
events that unfold when the Warrens sequester

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:09.740
the doll inside their Artifacts Room for safekeeping...only
to find out that her presence has some unexpected

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:12.020
and rather unfortunate consequences.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:16.590
"The doll, it's a beacon for other spirits."

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:20.780
In this movie, Annabelle and these other spirits
all pose a grave threat to the Warrens' young

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:25.619
daughter, Judy, as well as a pair of particularly
unlucky babysitters who've been tasked with

00:01:25.619 --> 00:01:26.680
watching over her.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:36.060
Attempting to describe the film, Conjuring
universe mastermind James Wan said:

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:38.939
"[It's] basically A Night at the Museum, with
Annabelle."

00:01:38.939 --> 00:01:42.659
The critics who caught preview screenings
of Annabelle Comes Home generally agree that

00:01:42.659 --> 00:01:46.850
the film is just as fun and over-the-top as
Wan's description suggests.

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:50.610
CinemaBlend's Eric Eisenberg claims that the
Annabelle series just keeps getting better

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:51.610
and better.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:52.610
The critic wrote,

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:56.280
"Excited I can now say Annabelle Comes Home
is excellent, solidifying the trilogy as a

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:58.509
rare one that improves with each sequel.

00:01:58.509 --> 00:02:03.130
The cast is fantastic, the monster mayhem
is surprisingly clever, and the whole experience

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:04.499
is just super fun.

00:02:04.499 --> 00:02:06.450
It's a big win for The Conjuring Universe."

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:10.690
Silas Lesnick of MovieBill was pleased to
report that the new crop of spirits didn't

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:13.379
feel forced, thanks to some smart narrative
choices.

00:02:13.379 --> 00:02:15.930
"I'm thrilled to report that [Annabelle Comes
Home] is great!

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:20.810
It has a smart script, fantastic performances
and it expands the Conjuring universe in some

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:22.110
really clever ways.

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:24.450
Mostly, though, it's just a ton of fun!"

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:29.239
Eric Francisco of Inverse was similarly impressed
with the film's array of supernatural threats,

00:02:29.239 --> 00:02:30.239
calling the movie

00:02:30.239 --> 00:02:34.540
"An atmospheric thrill that cements The Conjuring
franchise as THE horror movie universe to

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:35.540
reckon with.

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:39.010
There's plenty more than just parlor tricks
in the Warrens' forbidden room than you might

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:40.010
expect."

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:44.299
While Wan's Night at the Museum comparison
makes for an enticing blender pitch, Fandango's

00:02:44.299 --> 00:02:48.660
Erik Davis compared the horror film to another
quirky comedy, one which might make you even

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:50.959
more excited to see what the movie has in
store.

00:02:50.959 --> 00:02:51.959
He wrote,

00:02:51.959 --> 00:02:55.300
"[Annabelle Comes Home] is like Adventures
in Babysitting as a horror movie, and it's

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:56.599
a damn good time.

00:02:56.599 --> 00:03:01.010
The scares are never repetitive, the humor
is on point &amp; there are plenty of creepy entities

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:02.010
to freak you out.

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:05.480
Plus, I love movies where it's up to the babysitter
to save the day."

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:09.530
Finally, Dread Central's Jonathan Barkan weighed
in on the film, and, while he was careful

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:13.390
to avoid spoilers, he offered up a few general
thoughts on Twitter, saying:

00:03:13.390 --> 00:03:15.319
"Seriously, I loved this movie.

00:03:15.319 --> 00:03:17.980
Had a genuine blast with it and I can't recommend
it enough!"

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:22.469
Of course, he might only be saying that because
of the special guest he says he saw the screening

00:03:22.469 --> 00:03:23.469
with.

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:27.511
While the consensus may change as more reviews
come in, the early buzz is unanimous: Annabelle

00:03:27.511 --> 00:03:32.640
Comes Home is a bona fide success, and potentially
a high point for the whole Conjuring franchise.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:34.040
Take a bow, Annabelle!

